{"name":"Andiron","hex":"#424036","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"andiron","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A utensil for supporting wood when burning in a fireplace, one being placed on each side"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/andiron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Andiron","blocks":[{"text":"An andiron, firedog, fire-dog, fire dog, iron-dog, or chenet is a bracket support, normally one of a pair, on which logs are laid for burning in an open fireplace, so that air may circulate under the firewood, allowing better burning and less smoke. They generally consist of a tall vertical element at the front, with at least two legs. This stops the logs from rolling out into the room, and may be highly decorative. The other element is one or more low horizontal pieces stretching back into the fireplace and serving to hold the logs off the bottom of the fireplace. An andiron is sometimes called a dog or dog-iron."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Hand-wrought_Metal_Andiron_Set.jpg/330px-Hand-wrought_Metal_Andiron_Set.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andiron","wikidata":"Q262026"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Andirons_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Andirons_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Andirons_%28PSF%29.png/1280px-Andirons_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Andirons_%28PSF%29.png/500px-Andirons_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A drawing of andirons in use","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndirons_(PSF).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Pair_of_andirons_MET_ES3175.jpg/500px-Pair_of_andirons_MET_ES3175.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Pair_of_andirons_MET_ES3175.jpg/500px-Pair_of_andirons_MET_ES3175.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"French, late 18th century. Gilt-bronze fronts, with wrought iron behind","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APair_of_andirons_MET_ES3175.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Andiron_MET_12874.jpg/500px-Andiron_MET_12874.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Andiron_MET_12874.jpg/1280px-Andiron_MET_12874.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Andiron_MET_12874.jpg/500px-Andiron_MET_12874.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"American iron firedogs, 1770–1800. Hessians at 3rd from left","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndiron_MET_12874.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Jacques_Caffieri_-_Pair_of_Andirons_%28Chenets%29_-_1942.799_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Jacques_Caffieri_-_Pair_of_Andirons_%28Chenets%29_-_1942.799_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Jacques_Caffieri_-_Pair_of_Andirons_%28Chenets%29_-_1942.799_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Jacques_Caffieri_-_Pair_of_Andirons_%28Chenets%29_-_1942.799_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Jacques_Caffieri_-_Pair_of_Andirons_%28Chenets%29_-_1